  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P$ be the point $(2,0)$ and $Q$ be a variable point on $(y-6)^2=2(x-4)$. Then the locus of mid-point of $P Q$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BowbY",
      "text": "$y^2+x+6 y+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "srv0M",
      "text": "$y^2-x+6 y+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eyJKb",
      "text": "$y^2+x-6 y+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iPxQK",
      "text": "$y^2-x-6 y+12=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\mathrm{P}(2,0) \\\\\n\\mathrm{Q}\\left(4+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{t}^2, 6+\\mathrm{t}\\right)\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\nLet midpoint of $\\mathrm{PQ}$ be R(h, k)\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{h}=3+\\frac{1}{4} \\mathrm{t}^2, \\mathrm{k}=3+\\frac{\\mathrm{t}}{2} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{k}-3)^2=(\\mathrm{h}-3) \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}^2-6 \\mathrm{y}-\\mathrm{x}+12=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
